            "review_text": "Skaglia71\nCremona, Italy3729 contributions\n0\nWe will definitely be back.\nAug 2026 • Family\nThe five dots reward the overall experience even though the food was definitely good. Competitive prices for a light lunch. Attention: this is always real street food, so the five dots refer to establishments of this level. Don't expect a classy restaurant; here you eat on the sidewalk at steel tables, sitting on plastic stools. Exceptional. Whether it was actually mentioned by the Michelin guide as indicated on the back of the menu, I don't know... I have my doubts, but in the end, I don't even care. A must-try.\nRead more\nTranslated from Italian\nShow original\nWritten August 28, 2026",
