            "review_text": "inatree29\nMelbourne, Australia25 contributions\n0\nWill try to scam you if you’re a tourist\nNov 2018 • Friends\n15k for the tiniest portion of xoi (sticky rice) - but okay if it’s good that’s fine.\n\nAsked us if we wanted wing or drumstick.\nOpted for drumstick and surprise, when paying the price was 40k for each portion. Kindly reminded them that this 40k figure isn’t anywhere on their menu only to be angrily told it is what it is. Paid it just to get away from them.\nThey also put rice paper rolls on your table hoping you’ll touch them so they can charge you. Who knows how much for.\n\nI speak Vietnamese and would have gladly paid 40k if it was fair and tasty but the place reeks of (and by that I mean I heard them laughing about it) opportunistic scamming - so beware.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 20, 2018",
